WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.830
&gt;&gt;&gt; So this morning we are getting a much
clearer picture of how Florida governor Ron

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.670
Desantis plans to position himself as a presidential
candidate.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:12.420
The official announcement coming next week,
but he laid out these plans in a conference

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.599
call with big donors.

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.721
We will have much more on that in a second,
but there is also this new development that

00:00:17.721 --> 00:00:18.930
plays into all of this.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:24.010
His feud with Disney, the huge entertainment
company and major Florida employer announced

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.590
that it is canceling plans, they did this
yesterday afternoon, to build a new $1 billion

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.590
office campus in the greater Orlando area.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.680
Disney cited changing business conditions
as the reason for not moving forward.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.360
CNN's Natasha Chen has more on all of this.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.130
This is, what, like 2,000 jobs?

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.170
&gt;&gt; Yeah, John, 2,000 jobs.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:50.149
It was supposed to be a regional hub for parks
and resorts so some of the imagineers that

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:54.170
design all the stuff you see in the theme
parks, as well as some corporate jobs, consumer

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.170
[9:24:55 AM]

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.329
corporate jobs, consumer product, support
functions like finance technology, marketing,

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:04.330
communications, this was going to be at a
complex in lake Nona that Disney purchased,

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.510
just east of Walt Disney world in central
Florida and the move was going to take over

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:15.080
the course of several years and the company
was giving people some flexibility about this.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:20.090
I'm now hearing that some people who did not
want to move to Florida actually left the

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:25.280
company and found other jobs to avoid that
move and now it's not happening at all.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.780
About 200 people already did make that move
and so yesterday in a memo the chairman of

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.090
Disney parks, experiences and products says
they will work with those individuals including

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:40.869
the possibility of moving them back here to
Burbank in the southern California area.

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:46.380
Now, as far as reaction goes, governor Ron
Desantis did release a statement through his

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.370
spokesperson and I want to read that to you,
this was acquired by Steve contorno.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:55.619
He did say it was unsurprising that Disney
would cancel the project given the company's

00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:56.619
[9:25:56 AM]

00:01:56.619 --> 00:01:59.189
project given the company's financial straits,
falling market cap and declining stock price.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:05.780
Unsurprising they would restructure their
business operations and cancel unsuccessful

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.780
ventures.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.800
When we did hear from other local leaders
as well, Orange county mayor demings and the

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:18.250
Florida democratic party chair all saying
that this is really because of the desantis/disney

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:22.830
feud that they feel that they've lost these
Florida jobs.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.190
In the meantime the trump war room official
campaign account on Twitter also put up this

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:35.480
tweet yesterday quoting the story saying Ron
desanctimonious gets caught in the mouse trap,

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.810
the culture of losing continues.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:42.980
So this really played into the politics of
the moment and of course a lot of business

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:48.200
decisions went into this as far as what made
sense for the company, but you can't help

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.190
but see this in the greater context as well
of whether they will thrive as a business

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.019
as they are having this feud with the governor
of the state.

00:02:57.019 --> 00:02:58.019
[9:26:57 AM]

00:02:58.019 --> 00:02:59.019
governor of the state.

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:00.019
John?

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:01.019
&gt;&gt; All right.

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:02.019
Natasha Chen for you, thank you very much.

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:06.620
As we said, this is part of a much bigger
moment for Ron Desantis and the new developments

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:13.500
are last night he laid out his vision of a
presidential campaign to major donors.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.580
With us now from Florida, CNN's Steve contorno.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:23.590
I've been on conference calls with campaign
strategists that sounded like what Ron Desantis

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:29.150
did last night, where he laid out his case
for how he's going to win and he sort of made

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.510
it all about electability.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.260
&gt;&gt; Reporter: That's right, John.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.549
We know that Desantis has been meeting with
donors for several weeks now leading up to

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:40.080
this expected launch.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.030
One of the reasons he has been meeting with
them is to shore up their support because

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:48.379
a lot are concerned with some of his recent
moms and recent stumbles.

00:03:48.379 --> 00:03:52.010
There are Republican donors who object to
the fact that the state signed this six-week

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:56.980
abortion ban, they're concerned about his
waffling on whether he would support Ukraine

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:57.980
and

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.980
[9:27:57 AM]

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.629
would support Ukraine and whether this Russia
is right in this war.

00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:07.040
So he has taken a more direct role in assuring
these donors that he has a strategy to beat

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.459
trump and that strategy is to say, look, I
am much more a electable, especially in the

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:16.470
states that are going to matter in the presidential
contest against Joe Biden.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.840
Listen to what he told those donors according
to the "New York Times."

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:24.340
He said, you have basically three people at
this point that are credible in this whole

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.630
thing, Biden, trump and me.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:31.300
Two have a chance to get elected president,
Biden and me based on all the data in the

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.300
spring states.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.370
So not only is he clearly saying, look, it's
between me, trump and Biden in a way that

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:40.550
just totally dismisses the other Republican
candidates in the field, but he's saying trump

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.600
can't get elected and that's not necessarily
surprising to hear that from a candidate who

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.380
is trying to curry support, but Desantis has
really avoided going directly at trump throughout

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:56.850
most of this run up to his campaign and yet
here he is in very stark terms saying, look,

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.900
this guy can't get elected again, I'm your
best bet if you

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:00.900
[9:28:59 AM]

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:01.900
again, I'm your best bet if you want to get
a Republican in the white house in 2024.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:06.920
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I mean, it's very blunt language,
even more interesting coming from the candidate

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.759
himself, not a strategist there.

00:05:09.759 --> 00:05:14.770
So, Steve, where does this whole Disney thing
fit into it with Disney making this announcement

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:19.610
just days before Ron Desantis is going to
make it official that he's running for president?

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:24.480
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Well, it's just another sign
that this back and forth between Disney and

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.979
Desantis isn't going away.

00:05:25.979 --> 00:05:32.230
It's been such a huge part of his narrative
and on his terms, he wants to talk about Disney.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:37.639
He made it a whole chapter in his book, frequently
discusses it on the trail when in political

00:05:37.639 --> 00:05:41.759
events in Iowa and new Hampshire and all these
other states, but Disney continues to punch

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:46.910
back in a way that put this in a negative
light for Desantis, just as they did when

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:51.780
they outmaneuvered him earlier this spring
and suggesting that they are going to cut

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:57.530
2,000 high-paying jobs from the state really
is giving his opponents an opportunity to

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.130
ding him as anti-business as he prepares to

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.130
[9:30:00 AM]

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:05.590
anti-business as he prepares to enter this
primary, John.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.150
&gt;&gt; It will be interesting to see

